A||||5||mbramble||Fiero Radio Question||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||04-07-2001||12:14 AM||||When I bought my GT project car a couple weeks ago, there were two Delco radio/cassette players in the trunk.  One has the equalizer.  This one is obviously not a stock Fiero unit because it has the newer type connector on the back.  The tape player doesn't work, I think it needs a belt.  Everything else works great.<P>The other one is an 80's model -- from the connector on it.  Everything on it works great.  Sat around listening to an old Bob Dylan tape as I was hooking up the other one.<P>My question is do the Fiero units have red light digits in the display??  Both of these have green displays.  If the stock Fiero units had red, does anyone know if there is a way to change these???<P>Thanks,<BR>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||AkursedX||04-07-2001||12:17 AM||||I believe stock fiero radio's are a red display, at least mine is. <P>I have no idea how to change it though other than finding a radio that has it already||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||04-07-2001||12:18 AM||||The stock Fiero unit that was originally in both my 86's was green. (One 86 was bought new in 86) the only time I can remember red was in the late 80's. I know some Firebirds and grand prix's had red. But I'm not sure of the 88 fiero's<BR>I think the backlight of the faceplate was red but the clock/radio station display was green.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||04-07-2001||02:10 AM||||All the stock units I have seen and had that were original equipment have been back lighted in red. (displays are all green)<BR>I have access to convert them to red back lights, parts are rather pricy though.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||04-07-2001||02:57 AM||||Oreif and Indiana are both correct here -- all of the stock radios (1984 - 1988) (I have the standard, the equalizer w/knob tuning and the equalizer w/push button tuning all here in the shop) have green digits in the display. The plug in the Delco unit was changed from a 12 pin to the 21 pin plug in 1989 - the newer units we sell all have the red digits in the display along with the equalizer and either CD or Tape. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||04-09-2001||10:28 AM||||The red backlight comes from a red tint on the clear plastic plate that transmits light to the various buttons.  I got a radio out of another car and took the clear plastic part out and colored it with fake stained glass paint you can get at a hobby shop.  worked great.||||reg||1
